  "claim": "Chad & Jeremy, the English singing folk rock duo, were born in the town linked by rail to Kendal, named after a freshwater lake of the same name.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Windermere Hotel (Lake District). Sentence: Windermere Hotel , originally The Riggs Windermere, is a hotel in Windermere, Cumbria, England, located near Windermere railway station.\nPage: Windermere Hotel (Lake District). Sentence: The hotel opened at the time that the railway link with Kendal was established in 1847.\nPage: Windermere, Cumbria (town). Sentence: Although the town Windermere does not touch the lake (it took the name of the lake when the railway line was built in 1847 and the station was called \"Windermere\"), it has now grown together with the older lakeside town of Bowness-on-Windermere, though the two retain distinguishable town centres.\nPage: Chad &amp; Jeremy. Sentence: Chad and Jeremy are an English singing folk rock duo originating in the 1960s, comprising Chad Stuart (born David Stuart Chadwick, 10 December 1941, Windermere, Cumbria) and Jeremy Clyde (born Michael Thomas Jeremy Clyde, 22 March 1941, Dorney, Buckinghamshire).",
