        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d1d1d0a9-29f3-509d-a9f3-caf4628d02b5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Windermere, Cumbria; Bowness-on-Windermere; Kendal; Cumbria, England\n- Organizations: Windermere Hotel\n- People: Chad Stuart; Jeremy Clyde\n- Topics: railway development; town naming; folk rock duo\n\nFacts:\n- In 1847, the railway link with Kendal was established, and Windermere railway station was named \"Windermere.\"\n- In 1847, the town of Windermere took its name from the lake when the railway line was built and the station was called \"Windermere,\" even though the town does not touch the lake.\n- In 1847, Windermere Hotel, originally called The Riggs Windermere, opened near Windermere railway station in Windermere, Cumbria, England.\n- Windermere has since grown together with the older lakeside town of Bowness-on-Windermere, although the two towns retain distinguishable town centres.\n- Jeremy Clyde, born Michael Thomas Jeremy Clyde on 22 March 1941 in Dorney, Buckinghamshire, is a member of the English folk rock duo Chad and Jeremy.\n- Chad Stuart, born David Stuart Chadwick on 10 December 1941 in Windermere, Cumbria, is a member of the English folk rock duo Chad and Jeremy.\n- Chad and Jeremy are an English singing folk rock duo that originated in the 1960s.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "23097ad7-29ab-529f-ad19-9cafd047f688",
        "text": "Page: Windermere Hotel (Lake District). Sentence: Windermere Hotel , originally The Riggs Windermere, is a hotel in Windermere, Cumbria, England, located near Windermere railway station.\nPage: Windermere Hotel (Lake District). Sentence: The hotel opened at the time that the railway link with Kendal was established in 1847.\nPage: Windermere, Cumbria (town). Sentence: Although the town Windermere does not touch the lake (it took the name of the lake when the railway line was built in 1847 and the station was called \"Windermere\"), it has now grown together with the older lakeside town of Bowness-on-Windermere, though the two retain distinguishable town centres.\nPage: Chad &amp; Jeremy. Sentence: Chad and Jeremy are an English singing folk rock duo originating in the 1960s, comprising Chad Stuart (born David Stuart Chadwick, 10 December 1941, Windermere, Cumbria) and Jeremy Clyde (born Michael Thomas Jeremy Clyde, 22 March 1941, Dorney, Buckinghamshire).",
